The dashboard feed search filter was vulnerable to stored XSS through innerHTML injection when highlighting search matches in user-controlled feed content.

## Changes

- **New safe highlight helper** (`dashboard/client/feed-search-highlight.js`): Replaces innerHTML pattern with explicit DOM construction using `textContent` and `createTextNode`
- **Updated feed filter** (`dashboard/client/index.html`): Calls `renderHighlightedText()` instead of inline string manipulation
- **XSS regression tests** (`tests/e2e/xss-feed-search-highlight.spec.ts`): Validates IMG onerror, SCRIPT, and SVG onload payloads remain inert

## Before/After

```javascript
// Before: vulnerable innerHTML sink
content.innerHTML = text.replace(
  new RegExp(`(${escapeRegex(term)})`, 'i'),
  '<span class="search-highlight">$1</span>'
);

// After: safe DOM construction
window.feedSearchHighlight.renderHighlightedText(content, text, term);
// Internally uses: container.appendChild(document.createTextNode(...))
```

Preserves existing UX: case-insensitive first-match highlighting, clears on empty search.

